{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UajdDThybJrsBvCS53BqQX","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"categories:\\\\n- key: contamination_detection\\\\n  name: Benchmark Contamination Detection\\\\n  narrative: Methods for detecting training data contamination in LLM benchmarks,\\\\n    including RL-robust approaches\\\\n- key: irt_equating\\\\n  name: IRT Methodology & Equating\\\\n  narrative: Item Response Theory models, calibration, equating, and their application\\\\n    to LLM evaluation\\\\n- key: benchmark_design\\\\n  name: Dynamic Benchmark Design\\\\n  narrative: Approaches for creating contamination-resistant or self-updating benchmarks\\\\n- key: dif_methodology\\\\n  name: DIF Statistical Methods\\\\n  narrative: Differential Item Functioning detection methods, power analysis, and\\\\n    small-sample strategies\\\\n- key: item_generation\\\\n  name: Automated Item Generation\\\\n  narrative: LLM-based test item generation with difficulty control and psychometric\\\\n    validation\\\\nmeta:\\\\n  last_updated: '2026-05-21T01:40:38.004Z'\\\\n  total_papers: 16\\\\npapers:\\\\n  belzak2020smallsample:\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-20T17:30:00.000Z'\\\\n    added_by: director\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Belzak, W.\\\\n    bibtex_key: belzak2020smallsample\\\\n    category: dif_methodology\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    relevance: Parsimonious logistic regression with sum scores outperforms complex\\\\n      IRT models for DIF detection in small samples; directly applicable to our N=50-80\\\\n      model cohorts\\\\n    role: method-component\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    title: Testing Differential Item Functioning in Small Samples\\\\n    url: ''\\\\n    venue: Multivariate Behavioral Research\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    year: 2020\\\\n  hardy2026scalability:\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-20T17:30:00.000Z'\\\\n    added_by: director\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Hardy, M.\\\\n    bibtex_key: hardy2026scalability\\\\n    category: irt_equating\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    relevance: Nonparametric signed isotonic R2 scalability coefficients outperform\\\\n      IRT item diagnostics; lightweight pre-filter for item quality before our parametric\\\\n      calibration\\\\n    role: method-component\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    title: Efficient Detection of Bad Benchmark Items with Novel Scalability Coefficients\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.24999\\\\n    venue: arXiv\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n  kim2019fpc:\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-20T17:30:00.000Z'\\\\n    added_by: director\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Kim, S.\\\\n    - Kolen, M.\\\\n    bibtex_key: kim2019fpc\\\\n    category: irt_equating\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    relevance: Fixed-parameter calibration requires only N>=200 vs N>=500 for full\\\\n      calibration; core methodology for our bifactor IRT equating with anchor items\\\\n    role: method-component\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    title: Application of IRT Fixed Parameter Calibration to Multiple-Group Test Data\\\\n    url: ''\\\\n    venue: Applied Measurement in Education\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    year: 2019\\\\n  liang2026dvd:\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-20T17:30:00.000Z'\\\\n    added_by: director\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Liang, R.\\\\n    bibtex_key: liang2026dvd\\\\n    category: contamination_detection\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    relevance: Detects variant contamination via generation variance (AUC 0.73-0.74\\\\n      vs Min-K++ 0.43-0.68); complementary signal in our ensemble but untested under\\\\n      RL training\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    title: 'DVD: Detection via Variance of Generation Distribution for Variant Contamination'\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.04895\\\\n    venue: arXiv\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n  polo2026growingpains:\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-20T17:30:00.000Z'\\\\n    added_by: director\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Polo, F.\\\\n    bibtex_key: polo2026growingpains\\\\n    category: irt_equating\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    relevance: Uses multidimensional IRT with fixed-parameter calibration and 100\\\\n      anchor items for extensible evaluation (rho>=0.9); addresses score comparability\\\\n      but NOT contamination detection or item regeneration\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    title: 'Growing Pains: Extensible and Efficient LLM Benchmarking Via Fixed Parameter\\\\n      Calibration'\\\\n    url: ''\\\\n    venue: arXiv\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n  polo2026psnirt:\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-20T17:30:00.000Z'\\\\n    added_by: director\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Polo, F.\\\\n    bibtex_key: polo2026psnirt\\\\n    category: irt_equating\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    relevance: PSN-IRT analyzes benchmark quality via 4PL IRT; provides published\\\\n      IRT parameters for MMLU we can use in semi-synthetic validation\\\\n    role: method-component\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    title: Lost in Benchmarks? Rethinking Large Language Model Benchmarking with Item\\\\n      Response Theory\\\\n    url: ''\\\\n    venue: AAAI 2026\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n  tao2026selfcritique:\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-20T17:30:00.000Z'\\\\n    added_by: director\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Tao, Y.\\\\n    bibtex_key: tao2026selfcritique\\\\n    category: contamination_detection\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    relevance: Self-Critique/RL-MIA partially addresses RL concealment via policy-collapse\\\\n      detection, but remains individual-model-level; our DIF is group-level and complementary\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    title: Detecting Data Contamination from Reinforcement Learning Post-training\\\\n      for Large Language Models\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.09259\\\\n    venue: ICLR 2026\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n  wang2026fragility:\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-20T17:30:00.000Z'\\\\n    added_by: director\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Wang, H.\\\\n    - Li, H.\\\\n    - Ko, B.\\\\n    - Zhang, H.\\\\n    bibtex_key: wang2026fragility\\\\n    category: contamination_detection\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    relevance: Proves GRPO/PPO RL training conceals contamination signals (14-20pp\\\\n      AUROC degradation), motivating our DIF-based approach which operates on behavioral\\\\n      patterns immune to NLL smoothing\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: 9a5bf5d3c7116cc4a104c06599fbcef2d1b5abf3\\\\n    title: On The Fragility of Benchmark Contamination Detection in Reasoning Models\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.02386\\\\n    venue: ICLR 2026\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n  white2025livebench:\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-20T17:30:00.000Z'\\\\n    added_by: director\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - White, C.\\\\n    bibtex_key: white2025livebench\\\\n    category: benchmark_design\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    relevance: Monthly-updated contamination-free benchmark with objective scoring;\\\\n      no difficulty calibration or psychometric equivalence across updates\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    title: 'LiveBench: A Challenging, Contamination-Free LLM Benchmark'\\\\n    url: ''\\\\n    venue: ICLR 2025\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n  zhang2024gsm1k:\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-20T17:30:00.000Z'\\\\n    added_by: director\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Zhang, H.\\\\n    bibtex_key: zhang2024gsm1k\\\\n    category: contamination_detection\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    relevance: GSM1K documents 10-13% average accuracy drops from contamination; provides\\\\n      ground-truth contamination evidence and item-level effect sizes (delta 0.8-1.4\\\\n      logits) critical for our DIF power analysis\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ef62f95c16f668f031d649799cbd79081c6d2b0f\\\\n    title: A Careful Examination of Large Language Model Performance on Grade School\\\\n      Arithmetic\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.00332\\\\n    venue: arXiv\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n  li2024contamination:\\\\n    title: An Open-Source Data Contamination Report for Large Language Models\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Li, Y.\\\\n    - Guo, Y.\\\\n    - Guerin, F.\\\\n    - Lin, C.\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: Findings of EMNLP 2024\\\\n    url: https://aclanthology.org/2024.findings-emnlp.30/\\\\n    doi: 10.18653/v1/2024.findings-emnlp.30\\\\n    bibtex_key: li2024contamination\\\\n    category: contamination_detection\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: Provides web-overlap contamination labels for MMLU and other benchmarks\\\\n      via Common Crawl matching; primary ground-truth comparison for our DIF-based\\\\n      contamination detection\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: 32e11cf020021c225782a3b77b5cfed4ae8e14a0\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: literature-gap-fill\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-21T01:40:37.987Z'\\\\n  shi2024mink:\\\\n    title: Detecting Pretraining Data from Large Language Models\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Shi, W.\\\\n    - Ajith, A.\\\\n    - Xia, M.\\\\n    - Huang, Y.\\\\n    - Liu, D.\\\\n    - Blevins, T.\\\\n    - Chen, D.\\\\n    - Zettlemoyer, L.\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: ICLR 2024\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.16789\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    bibtex_key: shi2024mink\\\\n    category: contamination_detection\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: Introduces Min-K% Prob method and WikiMIA benchmark for pretraining\\\\n      data detection; key baseline whose limitations under RL training motivate our\\\\n      DIF-based alternative\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: 3422d5e0cdfdc935d6a84a1e3d3f96659265fe3a\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: literature-gap-fill\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-21T01:40:37.987Z'\\\\n  balloccu2024leak:\\\\n    title: 'Leak, Cheat, Repeat: Data Contamination and Evaluation Malpractices in\\\\n      Closed-Source LLMs'\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Balloccu, S.\\\\n    - Schmidtova, P.\\\\n    - Lango, M.\\\\n    - Dusek, O.\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: EACL 2024\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.03927\\\\n    doi: 10.18653/v1/2024.eacl-long.5\\\\n    bibtex_key: balloccu2024leak\\\\n    category: contamination_detection\\\\n    role: foundation\\\\n    relevance: Systematic survey of data leakage in closed-source LLMs covering 255\\\\n      papers and 263 benchmarks; establishes scope of contamination problem motivating\\\\n      our detection approach\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: 798feda076ad710df65d509a7884bd15937c8056\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: literature-gap-fill\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-21T01:40:37.987Z'\\\\n  dekoninck2024constat:\\\\n    title: 'ConStat: Performance-Based Contamination Detection in Large Language Models'\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Dekoninck, J.\\\\n    - Mueller, M. N.\\\\n    - Vechev, M.\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: NeurIPS 2024\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.16281\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    bibtex_key: dekoninck2024constat\\\\n    category: contamination_detection\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    relevance: Performance-based contamination detection via perturbation analysis;\\\\n      closest methodological parallel to our DIF approach in using behavioral patterns\\\\n      rather than memorization signals\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: literature-gap-fill\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-21T01:40:37.987Z'\\\\n  golchin2024timetravel:\\\\n    title: 'Time Travel in LLMs: Tracing Data Contamination in Large Language Models'\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Golchin, S.\\\\n    - Surdeanu, M.\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: ICLR 2024\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.08493\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    bibtex_key: golchin2024timetravel\\\\n    category: contamination_detection\\\\n    role: method-component\\\\n    relevance: Instance-level contamination detection via guided completion prompts;\\\\n      baseline approach for individual-item detection that our group-level DIF method\\\\n      extends\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: d6d0fd994f37b630f35945736b5e1bb198148404\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: literature-gap-fill\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-21T01:40:37.987Z'\\\\n  zhang2024minkpp:\\\\n    title: 'Min-K%++: Improved Baseline for Detecting Pre-Training Data from Large\\\\n      Language Models'\\\\n    authors:\\\\n    - Zhang, J.\\\\n    - Sun, J.\\\\n    - Yeats, E.\\\\n    - Ouyang, Y.\\\\n    - Kuo, M.\\\\n    - Zhang, J.\\\\n    - Yang, H.\\\\n    - Li, H.\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: arXiv\\\\n    url: https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.02936\\\\n    doi: ''\\\\n    bibtex_key: zhang2024minkpp\\\\n    category: contamination_detection\\\\n    role: direct-competitor\\\\n    relevance: Improves Min-K% with vocabulary-normalized token probabilities; key\\\\n      baseline whose AUC degrades to 0.43-0.68 on RL-trained models, motivating our\\\\n      DIF-based alternative\\\\n    abstract: ''\\\\n    semantic_scholar_id: ''\\\\n    verified: true\\\\n    added_by: literature-gap-fill\\\\n    added_at: '2026-05-21T01:40:37.987Z'\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 11927, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DXZjaXXhWcdxGyG3ygfUVM","session_id":"f077ac60-b5f3-45fc-82ab-a50de5ad3465","uuid":"88486eaf-5973-4238-9d86-3705bdf07af3","timestamp":"2026-05-21T02:17:14.939Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018wwMeRE8pPryWZLZbeDWFR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HkJqACspoJ5NeaQVjg5rfm","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2) for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept). Your focus: **novelty, positioning, and related work**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title**: \"Identifying Capability-Authentic Benchmark Items via Differential Item Functioning\"\n\nThe paper applies Mantel-Haenszel (MH) Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis to the METABENCH LLM response matrix (5,219 models × 12,508 MMLU items). The central reframing: DIF-flagged items are not \"broken\" but \"capability-authentic\" — they concentrate the discriminative signal that differentiates model generations. Key findings: 31.3% of MMLU items exhibit large temporal DIF, DIF flags anti-correlate with contamination (r=−0.478 on GSM1K), removing all DIF items barely changes rankings (ρ=0.997), and MMLU is ~3× larger than needed. The paper reports 12 experiments including multiple negative results (bifactor IRT failure, underpowered RL analysis, weak ensemble fusion, failed item generation).\n\n## Key Claims and Contributions\n1. **Capability-sensitive item identification**: 31.3% of MMLU items exhibit large temporal DIF, correlated with domain-level accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307)\n2. **Cross-benchmark capability validation**: DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, N=33)\n3. **Measurement efficiency characterization**: ρ≥0.972 even at 50% item removal → MMLU 3× redundant\n4. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000)\n5. **Comprehensive negative results**: 12 experiments mapping operational boundaries\n\n## Related Work Cited\n- Holland & Thayer (1988): MH procedure for DIF\n- Li et al. (2024): Open LLM Leaderboard contamination detection (web-overlap labels)\n- Polo et al. (2024): Growing Pains — IRT for benchmark evaluation, anchor items\n- Sinharay et al. (2006): Bayesian cumulative DIF\n- Oren et al. (2024): Proving test set contamination (Min-K%)\n- Deconinck et al. (2024): ConStat perturbation-based detection\n- Tutz & Berger (2016): Item-Focused Trees\n- Hendrycks et al. (2021): MMLU\n- Cobbe et al. (2021): GSM8K\n\nTotal: 9 references (very sparse for a venue paper)\n\n## Data Details\n- METABENCH repository: 5,219 models × 12,508 MMLU items (57 subjects)\n- GSM8K: 6,702 models × 1,319 items\n- GSM1K: 33 matched models\n\n## Experimental Results Summary\n- Core DIF: C%=31.3%, enrichment=0.96 vs contamination labels\n- Architecture stratification: C% increases slightly (33.1%), IRT fit poor\n- GSM1K: r=−0.478 (wide CI), N=33\n- Semi-synthetic: ΔTPR dose-response confirmed, cross-subject ΔFPR=0.000\n- Graceful degradation: ρ=0.997 at DIF removal → massive redundancy\n- IFT: 78% overlap with MH, smooth temporal trend\n- Cumulative Bayesian: power improves but FPR inflates\n- RL robustness: N=13, fatally underpowered, all tests non-significant\n- ConStat comparison: 18% overlap, orthogonal constructs\n- DVD: AUC=0.58, noisy, expensive\n- Ensemble fusion: AUC=0.64, DIF lowest weight (0.22)\n- Bifactor IRT: complete failure (non-convergence, all fit indices fail)\n- Item generation: poor calibration (ρ=0.18-0.34), 180 GPU-hours wasted\n\n## Your Task\n\nProvide a detailed review focused on:\n1. **Novelty**: Is applying MH-DIF to LLM benchmarks genuinely novel? Is the \"capability-authentic\" reframing a real intellectual contribution or just relabeling? How does this advance beyond Polo et al. (2024) Growing Pains?\n2. **Related work completeness**: Are important references missing? Is the positioning fair?\n3. **Narrative coherence**: Does the \"capability archaeology\" framing hold together, or is it post-hoc rationalization of negative results?\n4. **Significance and impact**: Would this change how the community evaluates LLMs?\n5. **Presentation quality**: Is the paper well-written? Are 12 experiments too many / creating confusion?\n\nOutput format:\n```\n## R2 Review: Novelty and Related Work\n\n### Summary\n(2-3 sentences)\n\n### Strengths\n(Numbered list, specific)\n\n### Weaknesses\n(Numbered list, specific, with severity: minor/moderate/major)\n\n### Questions for Authors\n(Numbered list)\n\n### Missing Related Work\n\n### Preliminary Score: X/6\n### Confidence: X/5\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14172,"cache_read_input_tokens":38929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14172},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f077ac60-b5f3-45fc-82ab-a50de5ad3465","uuid":"56446f37-d881-413b-91a4-a95f2e7ed3e6"}
