{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DewvmsV6gN7JG6hrT4mVtr","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/report.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Handover — 2026-05-21\\\\n\\\\n> 由 Agent 生成，每次状态变更后自动更新。硬限 150 行。\\\\n\\\\n## 运行中\\\\n（无）\\\\n\\\\n## 待处理\\\\n- plan_015_bifactor_irt: Bifactor IRT（1 general + 57 subject-specific factors）的 general θ 分层能将 temporal cohort baseline FPR 从 31% 降至 <15%，同时在 semi-synthetic 框架下保持 TPR>0.60 at p=0.5。Bifactor 通过分离学科特异性能力和通用能力，消除 subject-level 能力差异对 MH-DIF 的混淆。（准备中）\\\\n\\\\n## 近期结论\\\\n- **plan_004_gsm8k_cross_benchmark** (negative): GSM8K 的 temporal DIF (2023 vs 2024) 将展示与 MMLU 类似的 30-40% ETS C%，证明 temporal DIF 现象跨 benchmark 泛化。使用 METABENCH 其他 benchmarks 总分做 external matching（GSM8K 无 subject 分层），预期 baseline FPR 更可控。如果 C% 在同一量级 → DIF 作为 benchmark health diagnostic 的泛化性得到验证。 ← 基于 plan_001_real_data_dif_mmlu\\\\n- **plan_017_downstream_impact** (negative): 移除 temporal DIF-flagged items (ETS C, ~31% of MMLU items) 后，模型跨代排名更稳定（Spearman ρ 提升），且稳定性提升显著优于随机移除相同数量 items 的 baseline。这证明 DIF 不只标记 noise，而是精确识别了 problematic items，为 DIF 作为 benchmark quality tool 提供 downstream evidence。 ← 基于 plan_001_real_data_dif_mmlu\\\\n- **plan_016_within_subject_semi_synthetic** (success): 在 subject 内部使用 within-subject total score 做 MH 分层的 semi-synthetic injection 中，DIF 仍能检测差异性污染（ΔTPR > 0.3 at p=0.5）。这证明 DIF 方法在 subject 级别也有效，plan_014 的 38% within-subject C% 反映的是真实代际能力差异而非方法失败。 ← 基于 plan_014_within_subject_dif\\\\n  [plan_016_report](/api/workspace-files/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/plan_016_within_subject_semi_synthetic/report/plan_016_report.md) | [plan_016_dose_response](/api/workspace-files/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/plan_016_within_subject_semi_synthetic/data/within_subject_dose_response.csv) | [plan_016_revised_dose_response](/api/workspace-files/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/plan_016_within_subject_semi_synthetic/data/within_subject_dose_response_e6d86f.csv) | [plan_016_revised_report](/api/workspace-files/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/plan_016_within_subject_semi_synthetic/report/plan_016_report_fb64fc.md)\\\\n\\\\n## 趋势\\\\n成功 5 / 负向 6 / 失败 0 / 共 11\\\\n\\\\n## 下一步\\\\n（无活跃 idea，请通过 ideas.md 添加）\\\\n\\\\n## 资源状态\\\\n（无服务器配置）\\\\n\\\\n## 告警\\\\n（无）\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 2009, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01F6dyyRLxeeSfrL6WUfD7Yu","session_id":"f077ac60-b5f3-45fc-82ab-a50de5ad3465","uuid":"47172db7-b788-448a-93c4-7a4c171c13e0","timestamp":"2026-05-21T02:20:13.358Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0174uvAJvQxVa81ru8tAPB4X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E53GD7XtBFpdv4NkMQ7uD7","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2 reacts to R1's review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2). You previously reviewed a paper titled \"Identifying Capability-Authentic Benchmark Items via Differential Item Functioning\" focusing on novelty and related work. You gave it 4/6 (Weak Accept).\n\nNow read Reviewer 1's (R1) review below and provide your reaction: points of agreement, disagreement, and whether R1's concerns change your score.\n\n## R1's Review (Methods + Experiments focus, Score: 4/6)\n\n**Strengths R1 identified:**\n1. Scale and thoroughness (12 experiments)\n2. Semi-synthetic validation framework well-designed (dose-response, 5 seeds)\n3. Cross-subject matching as FPR control (ΔFPR=0.000)\n4. Sanity checks convincing (random split 0.18% vs temporal 31.3%)\n5. Honest negative results\n6. Downstream impact analysis: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=−8 to −49σ) — inverts naive expectation\n\n**Major Weaknesses R1 identified:**\n1. 31% temporal C% is fundamentally uninterpretable — cannot decompose into contamination vs. capability improvement vs. multidimensionality artifacts. Within-subject C%=38.1% doesn't resolve this either.\n2. GSM1K validation underpowered: N=33, leave-one-out reduces r by 22%, CI=[−0.71,−0.12], partial r=−0.385 barely survives α=0.05. Also possible difficulty confounding.\n3. Baseline FPR of 31-53% undermines practical utility — a diagnostic flagging one-third of items has limited actionable value.\n4. Semi-synthetic injection too simplistic — no sensitivity analysis on injection mechanism (partial flips, difficulty-dependent rates).\n5. Unidimensionality violation acknowledged but not adequately addressed — RMSEA=0.092, CFI=0.81, TLI=0.78 all fail thresholds.\n6. Architecture stratification (Exp 2) adds little.\n\n**R1's Key Missing Analyses:**\n- Null-model simulation for expected C% under ability differences\n- Item difficulty confounding in GSM1K\n- SIBTEST or logistic regression DIF on subset\n- Temporal cutoff sensitivity\n- Model count imbalance check\n- DIF flag distribution across difficulty quantiles\n\n## Your Task\n\nIn ~300 words, respond:\n1. Which R1 concerns do you AGREE are important?\n2. Which R1 concerns do you DISAGREE with or think are overstated?\n3. Does R1's review change your score? If so, in which direction?\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10449,"cache_read_input_tokens":53101,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10449},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f077ac60-b5f3-45fc-82ab-a50de5ad3465","uuid":"60779abe-33a2-4c17-882b-1d5c17fc464d"}
